  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Registered-Post Counter",
    "overview": "Every application travels like a registered consignment. Each office hop gets a round dated postmark. The live hop shows where the file sits and when it is due, and nothing counts as done until someone acknowledges it. The interface is a post-office counter. Paper sheets with letterheads and ruled lines lie on a beige counter in light mode and on a soot-black counter in dark mode. Warm black ink carries the text and the primary actions. Sepia stamp ink marks completion, and natural red appears only when work is late, returned or failing.\n\nDensity is moderate and register-like. Pages lead with one sheet that owns the next action, the delivery note. Under it come the consignment slip with its route of hops, and then a register of tables and folded disclosures for the supporting record. A fixed, very faint paper-fibre noise keeps large beige or black fields from looking flat. The system refuses the card-grid admin dashboard. Counts sit in a ruled sorting rack with slip piles. They are not floating tiles.\n\nThe palette is pinned to the user's rules. Light mode is a bright off-white beige with no muddy cast. Dark mode is near-black with a faint brown undertone. No green, blue, purple, olive, gold or brass appears anywhere, and status always carries text.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Beige paper or soot-black counter, warm black ink, sepia stamps, natural red only for late or returned work.",
      "Round dated postmarks with an ink-roughened SVG edge record completed stages and verified documents.",
      "Dashed lines mean pending or a perforation. Solid lines mean done or committed.",
      "Consignment numbers, dates, counts and clocks are set in JetBrains Mono with tabular figures.",
      "Paper depth comes from two soft, low shadows. The sheet that owns the next action gets the larger lift.",
      "One 5-band urgency ramp (calm, near, soon, today, late) appears wherever a clock appears."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Late Rule",
        "body": "Natural red appears only for overdue, returned, rejected, expired or failed states. Warnings and errors are borderless `bad-soft` fills with `bad` text, and they never carry a coloured side stripe.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Is The Accent Rule",
        "body": "No hue other than warm browns and natural red. Never introduce green, blue, purple, olive, gold or brass, even for success. Approved states use the ink-brown `ok` with text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sepia Belongs To Stamps Rule",
        "body": "Stamp ink marks completion and authority: postmarks, AD marks, rubber stamps and finished hop lines. Do not use it for links, buttons or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Franked Figures Rule",
        "body": "Any identifier, date, count or clock is set in JetBrains Mono with tabular numerals. Prose never is.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Faces Rule",
        "body": "Inter and JetBrains Mono, served from `/fonts`, are the whole type system. The app works offline, so it never uses a web-font CDN or a third family.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Sheet Lifted Rule",
        "body": "At rest, only the sheet that owns the user's next action takes paper lift. Everything else rests flat on the counter until hovered.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dashed Means Pending Rule",
        "body": "A dashed stroke says \"not yet\" or \"tear here\", and a solid stroke says \"done\". Pending hops, warn chips, pending rubber stamps and empty draft checks are dashed. Completed hop lines and entered checks are solid.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put the next action, its owner and its due clock in one lifted delivery note before any supporting record.",
      "Do mark a completed stage or verified document with a dated postmark, and a sign-off with the AD mark.",
      "Do use the single five-band urgency ramp everywhere a deadline appears, and hatch late fields on `bad-soft`.",
      "Do set consignment numbers, dates, counts and clocks in JetBrains Mono with tabular numerals.",
      "Do keep motion to the established set: stamp landing (320ms), hop drawing (320ms), page settle (360ms, staggered by 30ms), and the loading shimmer as the only infinite loop. All of it is disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "Do give every status a text label. Colour and border style only reinforce it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use green, blue, purple, olive, gold or brass, or any muddy beige or grey-brown cast in light mode.",
      "Don't use red for anything other than late, returned, rejected, expired or failed. Don't outline warnings or give them coloured side stripes.",
      "Don't lay out counts as a grid of separate floating cards. They belong in the ruled sorting rack.",
      "Don't add an uppercase kicker or eyebrow above a heading. Tracked uppercase is for table heads, sidebar group labels and mono letterheads.",
      "Don't use hard offset shadows, glassy blur on content, or a third typeface or font CDN.",
      "Don't use dashed strokes for completed states, or solid strokes for pending ones."
    ]
